      "message": "btw, in a fresh Chromium checkout, with `target_os \u003d \"android\"; target_cpu \u003d \"arm64\"` in `args.gn`, I have compared the build plans generated by:\n\n- `gn-old gen out/default`, where `gn-old` corresponds to GN before all the changes related to validations metadata.\n\n- `gn gen out/default`, where `gn` is the version built from this CL\n\n- `gn gen --experimental-collect-validations-metadata out/default`\n\nThe only difference is the command used by the `rule gn` definition (which corresponds to the generator target that invokes gn again on build file changes).\n\nThis confirms that, at least this configuration of Chrome doesn\u0027t depend at all on validations metadata.",
